==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} ''[[#Old Norse|fjórir]]'', from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*fedwōr}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*kʷetwṓr}}, the neuter form of {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{m|ine-pro|*kʷetwóres}}.

===Number===
'''fjórir''' {{g|m-p}}, '''[[fjórar]]''' {{g|f-p}}, '''[[fjögur]]''' {{g|n-p}}

# '''[[four]]'''; the cardinal number after [[þrír#Icelandic|þrír]] and before [[fimm#Icelandic|fimm]].
#: ''[[sjá|Sjáðu]]! '''Fjórir''' [[maður#Icelandic|menn]].''
#:: [[look|Look]]! '''Four''' [[man|men]].

====Declension====
{{is-numeral (fjórir)|}}

====Related terms====
* {{qualifier|ordinal form}} [[fjórði]] {{g|m}}, [[fjórða]] {{g|f|n}}

====Derived terms====
* [[klukkan fjögur]]
* [[undir fjögur augu]]
* [[á fjórum fótum]]

===See also===
* [[fjarki]] {{pos n}}

